  "notes": [
    "Every value is either printed in a cited source (confidence 'observed') or absent (null).",
    "Nothing here is interpolated or assumed yet. When a value is filled by inference rather than",
    "read from a page, its confidence must say so, and the UI must render it differently - the same",
    "rule already applied to MAY_CAUSE edges in the causal graph.",
    "Spend benchmarks are company-level, not ARPA-banded: SaaS Capital segments by funding type and",
    "ARR, not by ARPA. They are kept in their own object rather than forced into the ARPA bands, so",
    "no value is attributed to a segmentation its source never used.",
    "Percent-of-ARR converts directly to percent-of-MRR for a monthly figure: annual spend of",
    "0.08 * ARR = 0.08 * 12 * MRR, so monthly spend is 0.08 * MRR."
